<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Tiflis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived federation of Georgia, Armenia and Azerbaijan, proclaimed in April 1918, which lasted barely a month before breaking into three states.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Facing an Ottoman offensive and the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardahan">Ardahan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batumi">Batum</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transcaucasian-sejm">Transcaucasian Sejm</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tiflis</a> declared independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> on 22 April 1918, replacing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/transcaucasian-commissariat">Transcaucasian Commissariat</a> with a federal republic. Independence was declared reluctantly, mainly so that the region could negotiate with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> as a sovereign state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government was headed by the Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mensheviks">Menshevik</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akaki-chkhenkeli">Akaki Chkhenkeli</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikolay-chkheidze">Nikolay Chkheidze</a> chairing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a>. It negotiated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/empire-of-trebizond">Trebizond</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batumi">Batum</a> while Ottoman troops advanced. The three national groups had conflicting goals: Azerbaijani leaders sympathised with the Ottomans, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> feared them, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a> sought German protection.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As the Ottoman army pushed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a> declared independence on 26 May 1918, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> followed two days later, dissolving the federation. The Soviets later revived the idea of union in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/transcaucasian-sfsr">Transcaucasian SFSR</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/transcaucasian-democratic-federative-republic.jpg" alt="Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Sarang · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Transcaucasian_Federation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tiflis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Akaki Chkhenkeli, Nikolay Chkheidze</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Georgian; Armenian; Azerbaijani; Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>, <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Transcaucasian Federation, TDFR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=transcaucasian-democratic-federative-republic" aria-label="Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5769 690 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6089 946L6092 948M6089 946L6090 947M6089 946L6095 997M6089 946L6224 991M6089 946L6090 947"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 948h0M6090 947h0M6095 997h0M6224 991h0M6090 947